{#
  The keyword panel shown beside a template editor (§6.25).

  The list is CLOSED: a template can say exactly these things and nothing
  else. Anything else it asks for is reported at edit time rather than
  rendered as literal braces in a signed contract.

  Requires `keywords`.
#}
<details class="mb-3">
    <summary class="fw-semibold">Mots-clés disponibles</summary>
    <p class="text-body-secondary small mt-2">
        Écrivez-les tels quels dans le texte : ils seront remplacés à la génération du document.
        Un mot-clé sans valeur (pas d'organisation, pas de caution…) devient un tiret.
    </p>
    <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table table-sm">
            <caption class="visually-hidden">Mots-clés utilisables dans un gabarit</caption>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Mot-clé</th>
                    <th scope="col">Valeur</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for keyword in keywords %}
                    <tr>
                        <td><code>{{ keyword.placeholder }}</code></td>
                        <td class="small">{{ keyword.description }}</td>
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</details>
